  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>81fe42f806718f2cab03a55bbd0ecb3e</srcmd5>
    <version>0+git20260806.393430e</version>
    <time>1786304490</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to git snapshot 0+git20260806.393430e: new 'grok du' subcommand, tmux DCS passthrough so theme/capability detection works in a multiplexer, environment-based terminal light/dark detection, ACP version-mismatch reporting, protobuf debug redaction; project picker dropped.

Also answers the legal review in boo#1273104: License is corrected to 'Apache-2.0 AND MPL-2.0' and a Legal-Review-Notice comment records the audit of the statically linked crates. pdf_oxide is shipped but is MIT OR Apache-2.0 with no GPL code (its jbig2.rs is a pass-through stub whose only GPL-3.0 string is a comment naming the jbig2dec crate as a rejected option); the real JBIG2 decoder pulled in is hayro-jbig2 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT); MPL-2.0 covers cssparser and seven further linked crates; colored_json (EPL-2.0) is not in the shipped binary's dependency graph.

The generated grok-build-*.obscpio is no longer tracked - the spec builds from the .tar.zst, so it only duplicated 62 MB of sources per revision.</comment>
    <requestid>1370236</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="6" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>ddbb887305fa6c9524804637d4f8cef1</srcmd5>
    <version>0+git20260815.d6a22a1</version>
    <time>1786978675</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update grok-build to git snapshot 0+git20260815.d6a22a1

Upstream has no tags, so the package tracks a pinned git snapshot via
_service (obs_scm, versionformat 0+git%cd.%h). This re-pins from
393430e (2026-08-06) to d6a22a1 (2026-08-15), 8 commits.

All 8 upstream commits carry the same &quot;Synced from monorepo&quot; subject;
the changelog entry is condensed from their message bodies. Highlights:
grok-4.6 becomes the bundled default model, GROK_CONFIG/GROK_CONFIG_PATH
override the config location, session directories are now owner-only,
managed-MCP allow/deny matching and the auth straddle are hardened, and
two panics (list-pane out-of-bounds, &quot;grok inspect&quot; on a closed pipe)
are fixed.

Both downstream patches still apply (context offsets only) and were
re-verified against the new sources:
  * 0001-disable-self-updater.patch - get_installer() is still the sole
    source of the installer identity for all six update call sites
  * 0002-disable-telemetry-by-default.patch - resolve_telemetry_mode()
    is still the sole telemetry-mode resolver

Vendored crates were re-generated (cargo_vendor update=true, 1250
crates, 75 added / 71 removed). The licences of every newly added crate
were re-derived: all permissive (MIT / Apache-2.0 / ISC / BSL-1.0 /
Unicode-3.0 / BSD-3-Clause / Zlib), no new copyleft, so the License tag
is unchanged.

No change to boo#1271921 (CVE-2026-47128, nono sandbox escape): the
re-vendor did NOT lift nono, because upstream pins it exactly
(&quot;nono = { version = \&quot;=0.53.0\&quot; }&quot; in crates/codegen/xai-grok-sandbox/
Cargo.toml). The vendored crate is still nono 0.53.0, below the 0.55.0
fix. The bug remains open and untouched.

Heads-up on the License tag, which this request carries to Factory for
the first time: Factory currently has &quot;Apache-2.0 AND MPL-2.0&quot;, while
devel:tools has carried &quot;Apache-2.0 AND MPL-2.0 AND GPL-2.0 WITH
Linking-exception AND LGPL-2.1-or-later&quot; since rev 10 (Lubos Kocman,
2026-08-10, for the statically linked libgit2). I verified the substance
still holds - libgit2-sys 0.18.7+1.9.6 does bundle the full libgit2 C
sources, and all eight MPL-2.0 crates are still linked - and left the tag
untouched. Note only that rpmlint warns &quot;invalid-license-exception
Linking-exception&quot; (0 badness); Factory's own libgit2 package spells the
same exception &quot;GPL-2.0-only WITH GCC-exception-2.0&quot;. I did not change
it, since the identifier is the original author's call, not mine.

Built locally against devel:tools/openSUSE_Tumbleweed aarch64:
finished &quot;build grok-build.spec&quot;, rpmlint 2 packages checked, 0 errors,
3 warnings, 0 badness. No %check section (pre-existing; the upstream
workspace test suite needs network access).</comment>
    <requestid>1371325</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="7" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>c07f5df033512b23b4d39f9d29fb5767</srcmd5>
    <version>0+git20260819.19d42e3</version>
    <time>1787566255</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update grok-build to the 2026-08-19 upstream snapshot (0+git20260819.19d42e3).

Highlights: persistent &quot;Never allow&quot; permission answers for MCP tools and
web-fetch domains with remember_tool_approvals on by default; consent-notice
gating with server-side verification of acceptances; GROK_FORCE_LOGIN_TEAM_ID
to restrict login to a single team; automatic worktree garbage collection
behind a fail-closed safety gate; earlier two-tier interruption of identical
tool-call loops; a pager status line; and several panic/freeze fixes.

0002-disable-telemetry-by-default.patch was rebased (upstream moved
resolve_telemetry_mode, so it no longer applied at fuzz 0);
0001-disable-self-updater.patch is unchanged. No patch dropped, no shared
library, no SONAME change. The vendored crates were refreshed and the License
tag re-derived from the new vendor tree (unchanged); the spec's legal note now
documents why it carries GPL-2.0 WITH Linking-exception and LGPL-2.1-or-later
(the libgit2 C sources that libgit2-sys bundles and links statically).

Built locally with osc build --clean for openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64: green,
rpmlint 0 errors, 0 badness (3 pre-existing warnings).</comment>
    <requestid>1373245</requestid>
  </revision>
